  "question": {
    "text": "For positive integers $n$, if $4 a_n=\\left(n^2+5 n+6\\right)$ and $S_n=\\sum_{k=1}^n\\left(\\frac{1}{a_k}\\right)$, then the value of $507 S_{2025}$ is :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "LjrEI",
      "text": "$540$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "SB5pH",
      "text": "$675$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "rNIhp",
      "text": "$1350$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HwwUJ",
      "text": "$135$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{aligned} & S_n=\\sum_{k=1}^n \\frac{4}{K^2+5 k+6} \\\\ & =\\sum_{k=1}^n \\frac{4}{(K+2)(K+3)}=4 \\sum_{K=1}^n\\left(\\frac{1}{K+2}-\\frac{1}{K+3}\\right)\\end{aligned}$\n$\\begin{aligned} & =4\\left[\\frac{1}{3}-\\frac{1}{4}\\right] \\\\ & =4\\left[\\frac{1}{4}-\\frac{1}{5}\\right] \\\\ & =4\\left[\\frac{1}{n+2}-\\frac{1}{n+3}\\right] \\\\ & S_n=4\\left[\\frac{1}{3}-\\frac{1}{n+3}\\right]\\end{aligned}$\n$\\begin{aligned} & S_{2025}=4\\left[\\frac{1}{3}-\\frac{1}{2028}\\right] \\\\ & S_{2025}=4\\left[\\frac{675}{2028}\\right] \\\\ & 507 S_{2025}=675\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
